<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Balance Druids</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria your Hit cap is 15%. Spirit still converts to Hit for us, and now Expertise also contributes to our Hit cap. At 15% Hit, your spells will no longer be able to miss Raid bosses. This requires a total combined Spirit, Hit and Expertise of 5100. Normally we will have no expertise, although we sometimes have a small amount of it from gems. Reaching Hit cap is very important for us, both because of it being an efficient way to get DPS, but also because it makes the rotation more predictable.<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Gems for Balance Druids</span></h3>Gems are a great place to grab any Hit that we may be missing. This can be especially useful when aiming for Socket Bonuses, as <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76651/energized-wild-jade">
<img alt="Energized Wild Jade" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_green.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Energized Wild Jade</span></a> and <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76686/purified-imperial-amethyst">
<img alt="Purified Imperial Amethyst" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_purple.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Purified Imperial Amethyst</span></a> are the only good ways to utilize a Blue Socket if we want the bonus.<br/>
<br/>You will generally aim to fill all Blue Sockets, and then using reforge to ensure Hit cap. If you're still under Hit cap afterwards, then using <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76651/energized-wild-jade">
<img alt="Energized Wild Jade" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_green.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Energized Wild Jade</span></a> in yellow sockets is also an option.<br/>
<br/>Once you're at 5100 Hit Rating, things become complex. The general rule of thumb is to prioritize Intellect, while grabbing Haste in Yellow Sockets if you are below 8089 Haste rating without Tier 14 4 set bonus. If you have tier 14 4 set bonus or above 8089 Haste rating, you will instead aim to grab Critical Strike rating from Yellow Sockets.<br/>
<br/>There will also be situations where using pure Haste or Critical Strike gems is better than Intellect gems, this can however not be determined without a sim and so for the best results it is recommended to always sim yourself.<ul class="exclude-units">
