<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafting-professions">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Professions &amp; Crafted Gear for Balance Druids</span></h2>Nearly every profession in Mists of Pandaria provides a decent boost to your characters damage output. However, a few stand out for giving a bit of an extra boost.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="engineering">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_engineering.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Engineering for Balance Druid</h4>Engineering brings several gadgets and tools that can be helpful in your adventures. <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87215/wormhole-generator-pandaria">
<img alt="Wormhole Generator: Pandaria" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/sha_spell_fire_felfirenova.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wormhole Generator: Pandaria</span></a> will help you get around Pandaria quicker, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87214/blingtron-4000">
<img alt="Blingtron 4000" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_lilsmoky.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blingtron 4000</span></a> allowing you to repair from anywhere without having to go back to a town. In addition it provides the highest DPS boost out of any profession through <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126734/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shaman_elementaloath.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a>. And if all of that wasn't enough, it will provide a strong item for early gearing, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77535/camouflage-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Camouflage Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Camouflage Retinal Armor</span></a>. This item lets you choose your own secondary stats through the Cogwheel socket, letting you use 2 different gems like <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77541/smooth-tinkers-gear">
<img alt="Smooth Tinker's Gear" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Smooth Tinker's Gear</span></a> to make your perfect goggles!<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="tailoring">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_tailoring.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Tailoring for Balance Druid</h4>While you won't be equipping the things you craft with Tailoring, you will certainly benefit from <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=142173/lightweave-embroidery">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_thread_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightweave Embroidery</span></a>, an embroidery unique to Tailors. The enchant will provide a chance to gain a large Intellect boost when casting spells. This is generally the highest DPS profession for casters.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="blacksmithing">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_blacksmithing.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Blacksmithing for Balance Druid</h4>Blacksmithing isn't a profession to choose in order to craft gear you would use, but rather for the benefits of two extra gem slots. Blacksmithing brings with it the now traditional additional Sockets with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55628/socket-bracer">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_socketedbracer.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Socket Bracer</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55641/socket-gloves">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_addsocketglove.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Socket Gloves</span></a>, giving a flexible stat choice that can be very strong. Especially with gems in Mists of Pandaria providing twice as much secondary stats, Blacksmithing can help you reach your secondary stat caps.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted Gear for Balance Druids</span></h3>Crafted items are no longer restricted by profession, meaning that even if you aren't a Leatherworker, you can equip anything Leatherworkers craft. As a Balance Druid, some of the crafted items will even be Best in Slot until the later raids in Phase 1 release.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=98049/relic-of-yulon">
<img alt="Relic of Yu'lon" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_dragon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Yu'lon</span></a> is a very strong trinket, and will last us all the way until Terrace of Endless Spring as our best possible trinket. However, It is expensive to craft, but it gets the most use out of any crafted item we can get.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85829/nightfire-robe">
<img alt="Nightfire Robe" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_robe_leather_raiddruid_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nightfire Robe</span></a> is our second best chest until Heart of Fear. The best chest before Heart of Fear drops from the world boss Galleon and is therefore rare and hard to get.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85827/liferuned-leather-gloves">
<img alt="Liferuned Leather Gloves" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_leather_raidmonk_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Liferuned Leather Gloves</span></a> is our best gloves until Heart of Fear. Once we reach Heart of Fear, we are looking to get Tier gloves as quickly as possible however, so these might not last for very long.</div></li></ul>
